n## Key Implementation Details\n\n**ColumnParallelLinear:**\n- Splits the weight matrix by output features (rows) across ranks\n- Each rank stores `(out_features // world_size, in_features)` weight matrix\n- Bias is sharded along the output dimension: `(out_features // world_size,)`\n- Forward: computes local output, then `all_gather` to concatenate outputs from all ranks\n- Backward: scatters the full gradient back to each rank's partition\n\n**RowParallelLinear:**\n- Splits the weight matrix by input features (columns) across ranks  \n- Each rank stores `(out_features, in_features // world_size)` weight matrix\n- Bias remains full on each rank: `(out_features,)` (only added on rank 0 to avoid duplication)\n- Forward: each rank extracts its input partition, computes partial output, then `all_reduce` to sum contributions\n- Backward: gradient passes through unchanged (as in standard all_reduce semantics)\n\n**Custom Autograd Functions:**\n- `_AllGather`: Properly handles gradient scattering in the backward pass\n- `_AllReduce`: Handles the all_reduce collective with correct gradient flow\n\nBoth classes:\n- Accept a `master_weight` (full, unsharded weight) and shard it appropriately\n- Initialize biases to zero as specified\n- Work correctly with `world_size` values of 1, 2, and 4\n- Properly track gradients for both weights and biases","ttft_ms":98273,"type":"result","duration_ms":105402,"uuid":"aededdab-faa0-4d2c-9a7c-813fa9fc35f8","ttft_stream_ms":2460,"time_to_request_ms":41,"queued_turn_count":0}
